WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.108 --> 00:00:07.846
It was early morning, and Ray's house was still quiet when Ally sat up in bed.

2
00:00:07.847 --> 00:00:13.010
"I've got it!" She grabbed a pen and pad of paper from her bedside table.

3
00:00:13.011 --> 00:00:19.039
Alpha jolted awake. "What did you get?" She sounded worried. "A cold? A phone call?"

4
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.602
Ally laughed. "Poor Alpha, you're still not working right!

5
00:00:24.603 --> 00:00:27.434
No. I got an idea.

6
00:00:27.435 --> 00:00:33.232
I've already figured out going-away presents for everyone except Kate and Mateo.

7
00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.949
And now I know what to give Kate."

8
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:40.455
"Where's everyone going?" Alpha asked. "Are they moving away?"

9
00:00:40.456 --> 00:00:43.718
"We're the ones going away, silly," Ally said.

10
00:00:43.719 --> 00:00:48.768
"Remember? We're going to blast off to Carparia soon with Lainie Polk.

11
00:00:48.769 --> 00:00:53.215
I want to give all my Earthling friends gifts to remember me by."

12
00:00:53.216 --> 00:00:56.185
"Humans have insufficient memory storage.

13
00:00:56.186 --> 00:01:04.935
Advice: give them three billion gigabytes to increase their memory capacity."

14
00:01:04.936 --> 00:01:10.727
"I don't think I can do that, Alpha. But that's good to know."

15
00:01:10.728 --> 00:01:15.085
As Ally wrote down her idea for Kate, something else occurred to her.

16
00:01:15.086 --> 00:01:18.990
"Alpha's still not working well," she thought.

17
00:01:18.991 --> 00:01:25.011
"So I won't tell her yet that I'm planning to give Kate the phone that Alpha is stored in.

18
00:01:25.012 --> 00:01:28.426
Alpha might not understand and get upset."

19
00:01:28.427 --> 00:01:36.001
Ally picked up Alpha. "Since I'm already awake, I'm going to turn off your wake-up alarm for today."

20
00:01:36.002 --> 00:01:38.375
"A logical decision," Alpha said.

21
00:01:38.376 --> 00:01:43.017
After Ally powered down Alpha, she looked at the old phone.

22
00:01:43.018 --> 00:01:49.460
"Since Kate's always asking me about this phone, she'll love getting it as a gift." Ally grinned.

23
00:01:49.461 --> 00:01:57.221
"Now I just have to think of the perfect gift for Mateo!"

24
00:01:57.222 --> 00:02:03.623
Later Ally was working at the diner when Mateo came in.

25
00:02:03.624 --> 00:02:07.366
"How was soccer camp?" she asked.

26
00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:12.184
"Great! I just wish it wasn't ending when school starts."

27
00:02:12.185 --> 00:02:16.763
"School is starting soon? Yuck!" Ally said.

28
00:02:16.764 --> 00:02:21.341
"One good thing about being here is I don't have to go to school."

29
00:02:21.342 --> 00:02:26.490
Mateo laughed. "You don't like school on Astralia?"

30
00:02:26.491 --> 00:02:28.872
"It's fun to be with my friends.

31
00:02:28.873 --> 00:02:34.465
But I don't like all those tests and homework." Ally shivered at the thought.

32
00:02:34.466 --> 00:02:41.374
"Still, I'm so happy I'm going home soon, I might even be glad to go back to school!"

33
00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:46.339
"I like school, but I wish I could still play soccer every day."

34
00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:50.067
"Why can't you play after school?" Ally asked.

35
00:02:50.068 --> 00:02:53.937
"There's no soccer program until spring."

36
00:02:53.938 --> 00:02:58.096
"Then start one," Ally said.

37
00:02:58.097 --> 00:03:01.022
"I never thought of that," Mateo said.

38
00:03:01.023 --> 00:03:07.014
"Hmm . . . I'd have to convince Coach Cross to start a club or something."

39
00:03:07.015 --> 00:03:14.060
"Excuse me, miss?" A customer at the counter waved Ally over. "I'd like to order."

40
00:03:14.061 --> 00:03:17.029
"What can I get you?" Ally asked.

41
00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.945
"I don't know. What do you recommend?"

42
00:03:19.946 --> 00:03:26.685
"Toast and eggs are always good. And Ray makes the best huevos rancheros on Earth!"

43
00:03:26.686 --> 00:03:28.931
The customer thought for a moment.

44
00:03:28.932 --> 00:03:35.838
"I like eggs, but I don't like salsa. And I like cheese but not beans."

45
00:03:35.839 --> 00:03:41.718
"Let's try it another way. What are you in the mood for?" Ally asked.

46
00:03:41.719 --> 00:03:44.872
"I love salad," the customer said.

47
00:03:44.873 --> 00:03:52.477
"I've got it!" Ally said. "How about a scrambled egg with cheese—and a salad on the side?"

48
00:03:52.478 --> 00:03:57.845
"Perfect!" the customer said.

49
00:03:57.846 --> 00:04:04.184
After Ally put the order in, Mateo called her over.

50
00:04:04.185 --> 00:04:09.171
"You're so good at solving people's problems, Ally. They listen to you."

51
00:04:09.172 --> 00:04:12.680
"That's nice of you to say." Ally smiled.

52
00:04:12.681 --> 00:04:15.536
"My parents will like hearing that.

53
00:04:15.537 --> 00:04:19.019
Hmm . . . maybe you should write it in a note to them."

54
00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.180
"Sure," Mateo said.

55
00:04:21.181 --> 00:04:26.066
"In the meantime maybe you can help me convince Coach Cross to run a soccer club.

56
00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:28.439
We could play after school in the fall."

57
00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:33.645
"I'd love to! I have tomorrow off. I'll go to camp with you in the morning."

58
00:04:33.646 --> 00:04:38.258
"Great!" Mateo grinned. But his smile quickly faded.

59
00:04:38.259 --> 00:04:42.008
"I'm really going to miss you when you leave, Ally."

60
00:04:42.009 --> 00:04:49.490
"I'll miss you too." Ally started to feel very sad. "But we still have a few weeks."

61
00:04:49.491 --> 00:04:55.155
"That's true. I just wish you were going to be here for all the holidays coming up.

62
00:04:55.156 --> 00:05:00.137
You'll miss out on lots of parties and good food and presents."

63
00:05:00.138 --> 00:05:03.699
"What are the Holly Days?" Ally asked.

64
00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:08.275
Mateo's face lit up. "Thanksgiving is in November.

65
00:05:08.276 --> 00:05:13.036
And Christmas, Hanukkah, and Kwanzaa are celebrated in December, and . . ."

66
00:05:13.037 --> 00:05:23.478
Mateo's phone pinged with a text message. "I have to go meet Bethany. See you later."

67
00:05:23.479 --> 00:05:27.616
"Those Holly Days must be fun," Ally thought.

68
00:05:27.617 --> 00:05:32.413
"Mateo looked so excited when he was talking about them."

69
00:05:32.414 --> 00:05:34.807
"Aha!" she thought suddenly.

70
00:05:34.808 --> 00:05:43.528
"I've finally got an idea for the perfect going-away gift for him!"

